  "steps": [
    "Mix all the marinade ingredients in a bowl, add the chicken and turn to coat. Marinate 30 to 40 min while you prep everything else.",
    "Blend all the chipotle sauce ingredients until smooth and creamy, adding water a spoonful at a time if it is too thick.",
    "Heat a large skillet or grill pan over medium-high heat and lightly oil it. Cook the chicken 5 to 7 min per side, until an instant-read thermometer reads 165°F in the thickest part.",
    "Rest the chicken 5 min, then slice.",
    "Build each bowl with 1 cup of rice, the spring mix, tomato, corn, red onion and chicken. Drizzle with 3 to 4 tbsp of the chipotle sauce and garnish with cilantro."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "About 610 calories and 56 g protein per bowl with 1 cup of rice and 3 to 4 tbsp of sauce (creator's numbers).",
    "The creator uses lemon juice despite the name. Lime works too.",
    "The sauce makes about 1 1/2 cups, so there is extra for the week."
